    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0553" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg457"/>

                <head>No. 344.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 24, 1872</date>.
                        (Received September 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 614.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 272, I have the honor
                    to inclose a copy of a note which I addressed to Mr. Lafragua upon the 23d
                    instant, requesting the intervention of the Mexican government for the purpose
                    of restoring to their tribe in Arizona Territory the twenty-one Apache children
                    captured last year at Camp Grant.</p>
                <p>In a conference on this subject Mr. Lafragua promised to give this matter his
                    immediate attention.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d344-a1.xml" xpointer="d344-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
